title: Hyporenaemic Hypoaldosteronism
---

# Hyporenaemic Hypoaldosteronism

- **Definition** - syndrome manifesting as hyperK and metabolic acidosis due to inhibited renin-angiotensin-aldosterone axis, prevalent in diabetics
- **Pathophysiology of hyporenic hypoaldosteronism:**
  - <u>Mild diabetic nephropathy</u> - insufficient in causing hyperkalaemia alone
  - <u>Autonomic neuropathy</u> - impaired beta-adrenergic stimulation on renin secreation
- **Mx:**
  - Good glycaemic control
  - Temporary discontinuation of offending medications
  - Fludrocortisone
  - Diuretics
